1. How does your coded self-portrait reflect this year’s theme?
My portrait represents the person I am from my history of being born in Russia and growing up in North America. I represented myself as a Russian Matryoshka doll, and in the background, I have places where I actually grew up.
2. What was the inspiration behind your entry?
I depicted myself as a Matryoshka doll to show where I was born, but in my background, there is the Canadian Parliament building and the Space Needle in Seattle. I grew up in Canada, and for the past 6 years, I have been living here in Seattle, Washington. 
3. What was most challenging from a coding perspective in creating your project?
The most challenging aspect of coding was understanding how Bezier shapes worked, but once I figured it out, it became easier to make other shapes.
4. What did you find most rewarding?
The most rewarding was building my portrait, and then, in the end, stepping back and admiring my work. It was also very rewarding learning how to code in p5.js in general!
